From 35114db68b86c2eadbdd96a45bc9d23353bf160f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 13:39:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] release stale line boxes before collecting the areas to
 repaint

A phrase box logs its area for repainting when it is destroyed.  Two
caches of the series kept the lines of the previous typesetting pass
alive: the shove memo (its previous generation lived until the next
pass) and the merged stack item of a paragraph (kept after the paragraph
was retypeset when it became a single line).  A removed line was then
only erased from the screen at the next edit; typing a letter on a new
line and deleting it left part of the letter visible.

Drop the previous shove generation once the paragraphs are typeset,
clear the stack item cache when the lines are recomputed, and drop the
previous generation of line chunks after use.
---
