From 5435ff662a629d3baadd2180e42a97828d84dca8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:01:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] do not retypeset the whole rest of a document when a
 paragraph is removed

When a removed paragraph had changed the environment (a section, a
label, a numbered environment...), all following paragraphs were marked
for retypesetting, so that joining two paragraphs next to a heading cost
3 to 5 s in a 3,500 paragraph document.  Instead, the next paragraph
records the changes which the removed ones made at the previous pass,
and they are added to the old patch of the typesetter just before it is
typeset (edit_env_rep::removed_update): the usual comparison with the
previous pass then retypesets the following paragraphs as long as the
environment differs from it, and no further.  Blocks containing such a
paragraph are not replayed.  Documents with an accumulator keep the old
behaviour.
---
