From a7235d36419934a2db356b79e74ffbf7d924272a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 18:01:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/5] choose line chunk boundaries from the geometry of the
 lines

The boundaries of the line chunks (see "merge runs of lines into cached
chunks when floats are present") hashed the addresses of the line boxes.
Merging is exact wherever the boundaries fall, but after a full
retypesetting, which creates new boxes, other boundaries were chosen.  The
next commit rounds distances between the items of the body to the screen
pixel, and there the chunks matter: the layout on the screen would depend
on the history of the edits by fractions of a pixel.

Hash the extents of the line instead, so that the same lines give the
same chunks.  Since many lines have the same extents (full lines of
justified text, empty lines), a boundary is only accepted after at least
CHUNK_MIN lines: chunks stay long even if a common signature hashes to a
boundary.
---
 src/Typeset/Bridge/bridge.cpp | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/Typeset/Bridge/bridge.cpp b/src/Typeset/Bridge/bridge.cpp
index 67392b2be..1919fb96d 100644
--- a/src/Typeset/Bridge/bridge.cpp
+++ b/src/Typeset/Bridge/bridge.cpp
@@ -309,6 +309,7 @@ extern tree the_et;
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 
+#define CHUNK_MIN 16
 #define CHUNK_MAX 256
 
 struct line_chunk {
@@ -332,9 +333,16 @@ chunkable (page_item& it) {
 
 static inline bool
 chunk_boundary (page_item& it) {
-  // content defined boundaries (about one every 64 lines)
-  uint64_t h= (uint64_t) (uintptr_t) it->b.operator-> ();
-  h= (h >> 4) * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL;
+  // content defined boundaries (about one every 64 lines), depending on the
+  // geometry of the line only: the same lines give the same chunks, also
+  // after a full retypesetting (which matters for snap_stack_spacing)
+  box b= it->b;
+  uint64_t h= (uint64_t) (uint32_t) b->w ();
+  h= h * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL + (uint64_t) (uint32_t) b->y1;
+  h= h * 0x9E3779B97F4A7C15ULL + (uint64_t) (uint32_t) b->y2;
