From 2202a65fe63fe22ced3b80051dae9257a06375bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gli_acopo <82150202+GliAcopo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:14:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] move the pixels of unchanged lines instead of redrawing
 them

Outside paper mode, pressing Return or joining two lines moves every line
below the change, and the whole window below it was redrawn glyph by
glyph: 450 ms of CPU per key at 2560x1600 on long lecture notes (1.4 s on
a document with many figures).

Layout.  The distance between the origins of successive items of the body
is rounded to a multiple of the renderer's pixel (snap_stack_spacing, in
the merge of the document bridge and in the papyrus pager), so that all
items below a change move by a whole number of pixels.  Each distance is
off by less than half a pixel; paper mode and printing do not use it.

Detection (typesetter_rep::find_shift).  The typesetter keeps the items of
the body of the previous pass until the new body is built, so that
identity comparisons are meaningful, and releases them before
position_at collects the areas to repaint.  When the last items are the
same boxes, all moved by the same multiple of the pixel, it reports the
band that they covered, provided that nothing else was or will be drawn
in it: no other item of the body reaches into it (extents with ink), no
other part of the page (headers, footers, floats, notes, found on the path
from the root to the body) overlaps it, and page backgrounds are not
patterns.  requires_update then drops the pairs of phrase boxes inside the
band which moved by exactly that amount, and adds the moved images of the
other areas of the band.

Screen.  The editor asks the widget to move the pixels of the band
(SLOT_SHIFT_CONTENTS; QPixmap::scroll on the backing store in the Qt
plugin, where pending invalid regions inside the band are moved along and
the uncovered parts are invalidated).  It then invalidates the edges of
the band and the overlays drawn over moved text (cursor, selections,
search and spell highlights, environment boxes, loci, shown keys) at their
old and new places, and only the visible part of the remaining areas: in
a document with notes at the end, their union would otherwise reach the
end of the document.

Conditions.  Only with the Qt GUI, outside paper mode, for the first
typesetting pass of a change, with a plain document background, outside
graphics, and when the preference "move unchanged lines" is on (the
default).  With the preference off, neither the rounding nor the moves
take place and the layout is the one of trunk.  Other GUIs never receive
the new message.
